.DS_Store
# Formerly the whole multiqc_data/ directory was ignored here: MultiQC's fn_clean_exts
# has a "truncate at first occurrence of literal substring '.trim'" rule (meant for
# names like "sample.trim.bam"). FASTQC_TRIM's ext.prefix used to be "${meta.id}.trimmed",
# so both mates' zip names ("${meta.id}.trimmed_1"/"_2") got truncated at ".trim" down to
# bare "${meta.id}" and collapsed into one sample, silently overwriting each other with
# whichever mate MultiQC parsed last (varied per run) — 13 files inherited the flip
# (fastqc-1_*_plot.txt, multiqc_fastqc_fastqc-1.txt, multiqc_general_stats.txt, ...).
# Fixed by renaming the prefix to "${meta.id}_trimmed" (conf/modules.config), which
# doesn't contain the ".trim" substring. Verified deterministic across 3 consecutive
# runs after the fix; only the files below remain genuinely unstable.
multiqc/multiqc_data/llms-full.txt
multiqc/multiqc_data/multiqc.log
multiqc/multiqc_data/multiqc.parquet
multiqc/multiqc_data/multiqc_data.json
multiqc/multiqc_data/multiqc_sources.txt
multiqc/multiqc_plots/{svg,pdf,png}/*.{svg,pdf,png}
multiqc/multiqc_report.html
# FastQC outputs
fastqc/*_fastqc.{html,zip}
# fastp HTML report + log carry run timestamps (the .json payload is stable and snapshotted)
fastp/*.fastp.html
fastp/*.fastp.log
# Insert-size QC plot/data are non-deterministic (Picard CollectInsertSizeMetrics embeds run context)
QC/insert_size/*.{pdf,txt}
# SPAdes logs + its versions.yml embed timestamps / run-specific content (contigs/gfa are stable)
spades/*.spades.log
spades/*.warnings.log
spades/versions.yml
# samtools/versions.yml is non-deterministic: SAMTOOLS_IDXSTATS runs multiple times
# (markdup/withdup x major/minor) and each writes versions.yml keyed by its full process
# path to the same samtools/ publishDir. Last-writer-wins picks a different process-name key
# each run -> different md5 despite an identical samtools version. Same class as CR-01.
samtools/versions.yml
# NOTE: bowtie2/bowtie2/* used to be non-deterministic here (BOWTIE2_BUILD's
# per-sample index directories collided on publish, so which sample's .bt2 files
# survived varied run to run). That is now fixed at the source — the process no
# longer publishes at all (conf/modules.config) — so no ignore rule is needed.
# Pipeline info with timestamps and variable content
pipeline_info/*.{html,json,txt,yml}
# HCV-specific outputs that may have variable content
# Add any HCV-specific file patterns that should be ignored for stability